<div class="qr-scanner" hidden>
  <p>Enter the QR passphrase at the top of the page, the same as on the {{device}} device, and show the QR codes there. Then press Scan QR codes. The local server opens this device's camera in a new window with OpenCV, reads the QR codes in any order, and decrypts them once it has every one. The first time, the system may ask whether the terminal running the server may use the camera.</p>
  <div class="notebook-toolbar">
    <button type="button" class="run-button" data-action="scan">&#9654; Scan QR codes</button>
  </div>
  <p class="qr-scan-status" role="status"></p>
  <div class="qr-result" hidden>
    <h3>{{title}}</h3>
    <pre class="qr-output" tabindex="0"></pre>
    <button type="button" class="qr-copy">{{copy}}</button>
  </div>
</div>
